From 17a5d8bad50d5955037ff94fa3555b8e5b6b3a82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 02:05:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ImsStack: be the device's GBA service where the platform has
 none

ImsStack authenticates Ut/XCAP with GBA through
TelephonyManager#bootstrapAuthenticationRequest, and Android's default
GBA mode (gba_mode_int) is GBA_ME for every carrier. That request goes
to the GbaService named by the phone's config_gba_package; AOSP ships
none, nor does LineageOS, so every XCAP server that asked for GBA
refused call forwarding, waiting and barring settings.

ImsStackGbaService does GBA_ME (3GPP TS 33.220, Ub per TS 24.109):
- bootstrapping with the carrier's BSF (bsf.* carrier config, else the
  TS 23.003 default name) over HTTP digest AKA, AKAv1-MD5 with qop
  auth-int (RFC 3310), resynchronising once on an AUTS;
- AKA in 3G security context on the ISIM, or the USIM with the IMPI
  derived from the IMSI;
- Ks_NAF = KDF(Ks, "gba-me", RAND, IMPI, NAF_Id), HMAC-SHA-256 per
  Annex B, for each NAF, Ks kept until its lifetime ends;
- over the subscription's XCAP network if it has one, as ImsStack's own
  XCAP requests go, else the default network.
GBA_U requests fail with an unknown reason, on which ImsStack retries
with GBA_ME. The service is exported only to holders of
BIND_GBA_SERVICE; a device selects it with config_gba_package.
